# Agent instructions

> Copy this file to the **repo root** as `AGENTS.md` and fill in the brackets.
> For Next.js 16.2+, also follow the bundled docs under `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`
> (see Vercel’s AI agents guide).

## Project

- Name: [project]
- Stack: [Next.js App Router / Node Express or Nest] + [PostgreSQL] + [Flutter mobile if any]
- Package manager: [pnpm | npm | bun] — do not change lockfile tooling
- Import alias: [@/]

## Architecture

- Prefer Server Components in Next.js. Add `"use client"` only on the smallest interactive leaf.
- Keep secrets, DB clients, and auth checks on the server only.
- Validate all inputs at server boundaries (Zod / DTO). Never trust client identity, roles, or prices.
- Match existing patterns before inventing new ones.

## Commands

- Install: `[...]`
- Dev: `[...]`
- Lint: `[...]`
- Typecheck: `[...]`
- Test: `[...]`
- Build: `[...]`

## Working rules

- Follow Karpathy guidelines: think first, keep it simple, surgical diffs, verify with checks.
- Do not expand scope. No drive-by refactors or unrelated formatting.
- Do not add dependencies unless required for the task.
- After edits, run the narrowest relevant check; before handoff run lint + typecheck + affected tests.

## Security

- Never commit or print secrets.
- No `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` for private keys.
- Authorize on the server for every mutation.

## Never do

- [project-specific bans]
